IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sda-common`
IMPORT `fhog-terms`

-- First Home and Housing Construction Grants Act 2000 (SA), with the First Home and Housing Construction Grants
-- Regulations 2015 -- the first home owner grant. SEAT-NEUTRAL CORE: the rules are in the Act's own actors and terms
-- ("the applicant", "the Commissioner", "the Treasurer"). The buyer's questions are in sda-seat.l4, which IMPORTs this
-- module and restates no rule.
--
-- Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website (State of South Australia, CC BY 4.0), taken
-- through the Open Australian Legal Corpus (CC BY 4.0). The Act's deposited text is AS AT 2025-02-13 (scraped
-- 2025-03-10); the Current Titles list of 22 September 2026 lists a version of 4.12.2025, so a later version exists
-- and is NOT reflected here. The Regulations are AS AT 2021-03-11 (scraped 2024-09-13). Not the official texts; they may
-- be out of date. Grant amounts are encoded as the deposited text states them.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 7(1), (1a), (2), (3) (entitlement, the market value cap); ss 8, 8A, 9, 10, 11 (criteria 1 to 4,
-- with the "relevant day" an INPUT); s 12 (criterion 5, the residence requirement, regulative, with the Commissioner's
-- exemption or variation as INPUTS); s 13(1), (3)-(5), (7) (eligible transaction, commencement date, completion,
-- consideration); s 14(5), (6) (the application period, regulative); s 15 (all interested persons join); s 17(1),
-- s 24(1) (the Commissioner must authorise payment and give notice); s 18(1), (4a) (the amount); s 18BB(1)(a)-(c), (6)
-- (market value, for the s 7(1a) cap; for a building contract, the sum of the building price or cost and the land's
-- value); s 18C; s 20 (payment in anticipation of the residence requirement: notice and
-- repayment within 14 days, regulative); s 21(2)-(4) (conditions); s 25, s 27(2), s 28 (objection within 60 days,
-- review within 60 days, regulative); s 39 (repayment and penalty, regulative); s 40 (recovery); Regulations 2015
-- reg 6 (interest on repayment by instalments).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 6A (HomeBuilder grants); ss 12A, 12B, 18B-18BAC (bonus, housing construction and seniors housing
-- grants: four formulas are missing from the deposit); s 13A and s 18(2) (special eligible transactions of 2008-2009);
-- s 13(6) (moveable buildings); s 16 (guardians); s 22 (death of an applicant); s 23 (correction); Parts 3 and 4
-- machinery; s 38 offences except as named.
--
-- BASELINE. See NOTES.md. Not for public use as advice.

§ `First Home and Housing Construction Grants Act 2000 -- the first home owner grant, seat-neutral core`

§§ `s 13 -- eligible transaction`

-- s 13(1): "An eligible transaction is -- (a) a contract made on or after 1 July 2000 for the purchase of a home in the
-- State; (b) a comprehensive home building contract made on or after 1 July 2000 by the owner of land in the State, or a
-- person who will on completion of the contract, be the owner of land in the State, to have a home built on the land;
-- (c) the building of a home in the State by an owner builder if the building work commences on or after 1 July 2000."
DECLARE `Kind of transaction` IS ONE OF
    `a contract for the purchase of a home in the State`
    `a comprehensive home building contract for a home in the State`
    `the building of a home in the State by an owner builder`
    `some other transaction`

-- The facts of one application: one eligible transaction (the text's natural unit). Each "the Commissioner is
-- satisfied" or "in the Commissioner's opinion" is answered conditionally, as a fact. Where a criterion speaks of "the
-- applicant or the applicant's spouse or domestic partner", the fact covers every applicant and every spouse or
-- domestic partner (s 6: a separated spouse does not count). Terms borrowed from Commonwealth law (Australian citizen,
-- permanent resident) are FACTS.
DECLARE `Grant application` HAS
    `the kind of transaction`                                                       IS A `Kind of transaction`
    `the home is a new home`                                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the commencement date`                                                         IS A DATE
    `the transaction has been completed`                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date of completion`                                                        IS A DATE
    `the consideration`                                                             IS A NUMBER
    `the Commissioner considers the consideration may be less than the market value` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the market value as determined by the Commissioner`                            IS A NUMBER
    `the Commissioner considers the building consideration may be less than the actual costs to build the home` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the actual costs to build the home as determined by the Commissioner`          IS A NUMBER
    `the Commissioner is of the opinion it is a scheme to circumvent the Act`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `every applicant is a natural person`                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `every applicant is at least 18, or exempted by the Commissioner`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `at least one applicant is an Australian citizen or permanent resident`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `an applicant or spouse was a party to an earlier application on which a grant was paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that grant was repaid for a residence or condition failure, with any s 39(3) penalty paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an applicant or spouse could have successfully applied for a grant on an earlier transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an applicant or spouse held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an applicant or spouse held a relevant interest in residential property before the commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an applicant or spouse occupied that property as a residence for 6 continuous months` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the relevant day`                                                              IS A DATE
    `every interested person is an applicant`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date of the application`                                                   IS A DATE
    `the Commissioner allows the application outside the application period`        IS A BOOLEAN

-- Glosses. "the commencement date" (s 13(4)): for a contract, the date it is made; for an owner builder, the date
-- laying the foundations commences (or another date the Commissioner considers appropriate). "completed" (s 13(5)):
-- for a purchase, when the purchaser is entitled to possession and the steps to register title have been taken; for a
-- building, when it is ready for occupation as a place of residence. "the relevant day" (s 11(4)): "the day on which
-- section 4 of the Statutes Amendment (Budget Measures) Act 2025 comes into operation" -- not in the operative text, so
-- an INPUT (NOTES.md, finding 3). "the market value as determined by the Commissioner" is read only where s 18BB says
-- so, and is the market value of "the property on which the home is situated" (or "is to be built"), land, home and
-- improvements together (s 18BB(6)): for a purchase, when the contract is made ((1)(a)(ii)); for a building contract,
-- the property on which the home is to be built when the building contract is made, usually the land alone
-- ((1)(b)(ii)); for an owner builder, when the transaction is completed ((1)(c)). The building contract's actual costs
-- as the Commissioner determines them are read only where the Commissioner considers the price too low ((1)(b)(i)(B)).

-- s 13(1), with s 13(3): a contract that "forms part of a scheme to circumvent limitations on, or requirements
-- affecting, eligibility" is not an eligible transaction (the Commissioner's opinion, a fact).
`the first day of the scheme (s 13(1))` MEANS YMD 2000 7 1

GIVEN `g` IS A `Grant application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transaction is an eligible transaction (s 13)` IF
        (CONSIDER `g`'s `the kind of transaction`
         WHEN `some other transaction` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE)
    AND ((`g`'s `the commencement date`) `is on or after` `the first day of the scheme (s 13(1))`)
    AND (NOT (`g`'s `the Commissioner is of the opinion it is a scheme to circumvent the Act`))

-- s 3: "new home transaction means an eligible transaction that is -- (a) a contract for the purchase of a new home; or
-- (b) a comprehensive home building contract for a new home; or (c) the building of a new home by an owner builder".
GIVEN `g` IS A `Grant application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a new home transaction (s 3)` IF
        `the transaction is an eligible transaction (s 13)` `g`
    AND `g`'s `the home is a new home`

§§ `ss 8-11 -- eligibility criteria 1 to 4`

-- s 8: "An applicant for a first home owner grant must be a natural person."
-- s 8A(1): "must be at least 18 years of age"; (2): the Commissioner may exempt (a fact).
-- s 9(1): "must be an Australian citizen or a permanent resident"; (2): of joint applicants, one is enough.
GIVEN `g` IS A `Grant application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `criteria 1, 1A and 2 are met (ss 8, 8A, 9)` IF
        `g`'s `every applicant is a natural person`
    AND `g`'s `every applicant is at least 18, or exempted by the Commissioner`
    AND `g`'s `at least one applicant is an Australian citizen or permanent resident`

-- s 10(1): ineligible if "(a) the applicant or the applicant's spouse or domestic partner has been a party to an earlier
-- application under this Act or a corresponding law; and (b) a grant was paid on the application." (2): not if "(a) the
-- grant was later paid back; and (b) the basis for the repayment ... was a failure to comply with the residence
-- requirement or any conditions ...; and (c) any penalty amount payable under section 39(3) ... has been paid."
-- (3): also ineligible if the applicant or spouse "could have successfully applied ... in respect of an earlier
-- transaction ... but did not do so" (or could have, had they then been a citizen or permanent resident).
GIVEN `g` IS A `Grant application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `criterion 3 is met (s 10)` IF
        (    (NOT (`g`'s `an applicant or spouse was a party to an earlier application on which a grant was paid`))
         OR  `g`'s `that grant was repaid for a residence or condition failure, with any s 39(3) penalty paid`)
    AND (NOT (`g`'s `an applicant or spouse could have successfully applied for a grant on an earlier transaction`))

-- s 11(1): ineligible if the applicant or spouse "has, before 1 July 2000, held -- (a) a relevant interest in
-- residential property in South Australia; or (b) ... in another State or a Territory". (3): "also ineligible if, before
-- the commencement date of the eligible transaction, the applicant or the applicant's spouse or domestic partner --
-- (a) held a relevant interest in residential property ...; and (b) if the commencement date of the eligible transaction
-- is before the relevant day, occupied the property as a place of residence for a continuous period of at least 6
-- months." So from the relevant day, holding a relevant interest is enough to disqualify, lived in or not.
GIVEN `g` IS A `Grant application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `criterion 4 is met (s 11)` IF
        (NOT (`g`'s `an applicant or spouse held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000`))
    AND (NOT (    `g`'s `an applicant or spouse held a relevant interest in residential property before the commencement date`
              AND (   ((`g`'s `the commencement date`) `is on or after` (`g`'s `the relevant day`))
                   OR `g`'s `an applicant or spouse occupied that property as a residence for 6 continuous months`)))

GIVEN `g` IS A `Grant application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `criteria 1 to 4 are met` IF
        `criteria 1, 1A and 2 are met (ss 8, 8A, 9)` `g`
    AND `criterion 3 is met (s 10)` `g`
    AND `criterion 4 is met (s 11)` `g`

§§ `s 14(5), (6) and s 15 -- the application`

-- s 14(5): "An application may only be made within a period (the application period) -- (a) commencing on the
-- commencement date of the eligible transaction ...; and (b) ending 12 months after the completion of the eligible
-- transaction". (6): "the Commissioner has a discretion to allow an application before or after the application
-- period." The period's end needs completion; before completion its end is not yet fixed.
GIVEN `the date of completion` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to apply (s 14(5)(b))` MEANS
    `months after` 12 `the date of completion`

GIVEN `g` IS A `Grant application`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the application period (s 14(5))` MEANS
    `the last day to apply (s 14(5)(b))` (`g`'s `the date of completion`)

GIVEN `g` IS A `Grant application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application is made within the application period (s 14(5), (6))` IF
        (    ((`g`'s `the date of the application`) `is on or after` (`g`'s `the commencement date`))
         AND (   (NOT (`g`'s `the transaction has been completed`))
              OR ((`g`'s `the date of the application`) `is on or before` (`the last day of the application period (s 14(5))` `g`))))
    OR  `g`'s `the Commissioner allows the application outside the application period`

-- s 15(1): "All interested persons must be applicants." (2): "An interested person is a person who is, or will be, on
-- completion of the eligible transaction ..., an owner of the relevant home" (regs 2015, reg 5, exclude the South
-- Australian Housing Trust and, for a reg 4 interest, a registered proprietor).

§§ `s 18BB and s 7(1a) -- the market value cap`

-- s 18BB(1)(a): for a contract to purchase, "(i) unless subparagraph (ii) applies -- the consideration for the eligible
-- transaction; (ii) if the Commissioner considers that the consideration ... may be less than the market value -- the
-- market value of the property on which the home is situated, as at the time when the contract is made, as determined
-- by the Commissioner". (b): for a comprehensive home building contract, "the sum of the following: (i) -- (A) unless
-- subsubparagraph (B) applies -- the consideration for the comprehensive home building contract under section 13(7);
-- (B) if the Commissioner considers that the total consideration payable for the relevant building work may be less
-- than the actual costs to build the home -- the actual costs to build the home, as determined by the Commissioner ...;
-- and (ii) the market value of the property on which the home is to be built, as at the time when the building contract
-- is made, as determined by the Commissioner". (c): for an owner builder, "the market value of the property on which the
-- home is situated, as at the time when the eligible transaction is completed, as determined by the Commissioner".
-- (6): "the market value of any property on which a home is situated ... [is] the market value of the land, the home
-- and any other improvements". s 13(7)(b): the consideration for a building contract is "the total consideration
-- payable for the building work". (2) (a genuine farm) and (3) (a s 5(4) interest) are NOT ENCODED.
GIVEN `g` IS A `Grant application`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the market value of the home (s 18BB)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `g`'s `the kind of transaction`
    WHEN `a contract for the purchase of a home in the State` THEN
        IF `g`'s `the Commissioner considers the consideration may be less than the market value`
        THEN `g`'s `the market value as determined by the Commissioner`
        ELSE `g`'s `the consideration`
    WHEN `a comprehensive home building contract for a home in the State` THEN
            (IF `g`'s `the Commissioner considers the building consideration may be less than the actual costs to build the home`
             THEN `g`'s `the actual costs to build the home as determined by the Commissioner`
             ELSE `g`'s `the consideration`)
        PLUS `g`'s `the market value as determined by the Commissioner`
    OTHERWISE `g`'s `the market value as determined by the Commissioner`

-- s 7(1a): "if -- (a) the commencement date ... is on or after 17 September 2010; and (b) the market value of the home
-- ... exceeds -- (i) where the commencement date ... is on or after 17 September 2010 but before 15 June 2023 --
-- $575 000; or (ia) where the commencement date ... is on or after 15 June 2023 but before 6 June 2024 -- $650 000; or
-- (ii) if an amount ... is prescribed by regulation for the purposes of this paragraph -- that amount, no first home owner
-- grant is payable". The deposited Regulations 2015 prescribe no amount. So from 6 June 2024 there is NO cap.
DECLARE `Market value cap` IS ONE OF
    `no cap`
    `a cap of` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `g` IS A `Grant application`
GIVETH A `Market value cap`
`the market value cap (s 7(1a))` MEANS
    IF `day` `is before` (YMD 2010 9 17)
    THEN `no cap`
    ELSE IF `day` `is before` (YMD 2023 6 15)
         THEN `a cap of` 575000
         ELSE IF `day` `is before` (YMD 2024 6 6)
              THEN `a cap of` 650000
              ELSE `no cap`
    WHERE
        `day` MEANS `g`'s `the commencement date`

GIVEN `g` IS A `Grant application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the market value is within the cap (s 7(1a))` IF
    CONSIDER `the market value cap (s 7(1a))` `g`
    WHEN `no cap` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a cap of` `cap` THEN `the market value of the home (s 18BB)` `g` AT MOST `cap`

§§ `s 7 -- entitlement`

-- s 7(1): "A first home owner grant is payable on an application under this Act if -- (a) the applicant or, if there are
-- 2 or more of them, each of the applicants complies with the eligibility criteria; and (b) the transaction for which the
-- grant is sought -- (i) is an eligible transaction; and (ii) has been completed." Criterion 5 (the residence
-- requirement, s 12) lies in the future at the decision: s 20(1) lets the Commissioner pay "in anticipation of
-- compliance with the residence requirement if ... satisfied that each applicant who is required to comply ... intends to
-- so comply". So the grant is payable now if criteria 1 to 4 are met and either the residence requirement has been met
-- or the Commissioner pays in anticipation (both facts). s 7(3): "Only 1 first home owner grant is payable for the same
-- eligible transaction."
GIVEN `g` IS A `Grant application`
      `the residence requirement has been complied with, or the Commissioner pays in anticipation of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first home owner grant is payable (s 7)` IF
        `criteria 1 to 4 are met` `g`
    AND `the residence requirement has been complied with, or the Commissioner pays in anticipation of it`
    AND `the transaction is an eligible transaction (s 13)` `g`
    AND `g`'s `the transaction has been completed`
    AND `the market value is within the cap (s 7(1a))` `g`
    AND `g`'s `every interested person is an applicant`
    AND `the application is made within the application period (s 14(5), (6))` `g`

§§ `s 18 -- amount of the grant`

-- s 18(1): "the amount of a first home owner grant is the lesser of the following: (a) the consideration for the
-- eligible transaction; (b) -- (i) in the case of an eligible transaction other than a new home transaction -- (A) if the
-- commencement date ... is before the 2012 statutory date -- $7 000; and (B) ... between the 2012 statutory date and
-- 30 June 2014 (both dates inclusive) -- $5 000; (ii) in the case of ... a new home transaction -- (A) if the commencement
-- date ... is before 15 October 2012 -- $7 000; and (B) ... on or after 15 October 2012 -- $15 000." (4a): "a first home
-- owner grant is not payable under this section in relation to a contract made on or after 1 July 2014 unless the
-- contract is a new home transaction." For a transaction other than a new home transaction commencing after 30 June 2014,
-- s 18(1)(b)(i) gives no amount at all, so nothing is payable for an owner builder or building contract either.
-- COVERED: a new home transaction commencing on or after 15 October 2012; any other transaction commencing on or after
-- 1 July 2014. Earlier: `not covered` (the bonus grants of ss 18B, 18BA have lost formulas; the 2012 statutory date is
-- not in the operative text).
`the new home grant amount (s 18(1)(b)(ii)(B))` MEANS 15000

GIVEN `g` IS A `Grant application`
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
`the amount of the first home owner grant (s 18)` MEANS
    IF `it is a new home transaction (s 3)` `g`
    THEN IF ((`g`'s `the commencement date`) `is on or after` (YMD 2012 10 15))
         THEN `the amount, in dollars, is` (`the lesser of` (`g`'s `the consideration`) `the new home grant amount (s 18(1)(b)(ii)(B))`)
         ELSE `not covered` `the grant amounts before 15 October 2012 involve bonus grants whose formulas are missing (ss 18B, 18BA) and are not encoded`
    ELSE IF ((`g`'s `the commencement date`) `is on or after` (YMD 2014 7 1))
         THEN `the amount, in dollars, is` 0
         ELSE `not covered` `the grant amount for a transaction other than a new home transaction before 1 July 2014 turns on the 2012 statutory date and is not encoded`

-- The grant on an application, as one answer: the s 18 amount if the grant is payable under s 7, otherwise nothing.
GIVEN `g` IS A `Grant application`
      `the residence requirement has been complied with, or the Commissioner pays in anticipation of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
`the first home owner grant payable on the application (ss 7, 18)` MEANS
    IF `the first home owner grant is payable (s 7)` `g` `the residence requirement has been complied with, or the Commissioner pays in anticipation of it`
    THEN `the amount of the first home owner grant (s 18)` `g`
    ELSE `the amount, in dollars, is` 0

-- s 18C: if additional grants would take "the total amount payable in relation to a home" above "the consideration for
-- the eligible transaction", they are adjusted so the total equals the consideration. Of those grants only the s 18
-- grant is encoded, and s 18(1)(a) already holds it to the consideration.
GIVEN `the total of the grants` IS A NUMBER, `the consideration` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total grants payable after s 18C` MEANS
    `the lesser of` `the total of the grants` `the consideration`

§§ `s 12 and s 20 -- the residence requirement and payment in anticipation (regulative)`

-- s 12(1): "An applicant for a first home owner grant must occupy the home to which the application relates as the
-- applicant's principal place of residence for a continuous period of at least 6 months (or a shorter period approved by
-- the Commissioner) (the residence period), commencing within 12 months after completion of the eligible transaction (or
-- within a longer period approved by the Commissioner) (the completion period)." (2): the Commissioner may exempt one of
-- joint applicants if at least one complies and there are good reasons. (3), (4): the Commissioner may vary the
-- requirement, and the varied requirement is taken to have applied from the determination. Exemption and variation are
-- INPUTS.
`the residence period, in months (s 12(1))` MEANS 6
`the completion period, in months (s 12(1))` MEANS 12

GIVEN `the date of completion` IS A DATE
      `a longer completion period approved by the Commissioner, in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to begin living in the home (s 12)` MEANS
    `months after` (`the greater of` `the completion period, in months (s 12(1))` `a longer completion period approved by the Commissioner, in months`) `the date of completion`

GIVEN `the day the applicant began living there` IS A DATE
      `a shorter residence period approved by the Commissioner, in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the residence period ends (s 12)` MEANS
    `months after` `months` `the day the applicant began living there`
    WHERE
        `months` MEANS
            IF `a shorter residence period approved by the Commissioner, in months` GREATER THAN 0
            THEN `the lesser of` `a shorter residence period approved by the Commissioner, in months` `the residence period, in months (s 12(1))`
            ELSE `the residence period, in months (s 12(1))`

-- s 20(2): "If a first home owner grant is paid in anticipation of compliance with the residence requirement, the
-- payment is made on condition that, if the residence requirement is not complied with, the applicant must within 14
-- days after the relevant date -- (a) give written notice of that fact to the Commissioner; and (b) repay the amount of
-- the grant." (3): "The relevant date is the earlier of ... (a) the end of the period allowed for compliance ...; (b) the
-- date on which it first becomes apparent that the residence requirement will not be complied with". (4): failure is an
-- offence, "Maximum penalty: $5 000". s 21(3): of joint applicants each is liable, and compliance by one is compliance
-- by all. s 39(3): failing to repay, the Commissioner "may, by written notice, impose a penalty not exceeding the amount
-- the applicant is required to repay".
`the days to notify and repay (s 20(2))` MEANS 14
`the maximum fine for not notifying and repaying (s 20(4))` MEANS 5000

-- s 20(3)(a), "the end of the period allowed for compliance with the residence requirement": READING (NOTES.md,
-- finding 16) the day a residence period begun on the last day allowed would end -- the last day on which the
-- requirement can still be met.
GIVEN `the date of completion` IS A DATE
      `a longer completion period approved by the Commissioner, in months` IS A NUMBER
      `a shorter residence period approved by the Commissioner, in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the end of the period allowed for compliance (s 20(3)(a))` MEANS
    `the day the residence period ends (s 12)` (`the last day to begin living in the home (s 12)` `the date of completion` `a longer completion period approved by the Commissioner, in months`) `a shorter residence period approved by the Commissioner, in months`

GIVEN `the end of the period allowed for compliance` IS A DATE
      `the date it first becomes apparent the requirement will not be complied with` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to notify and repay (s 20(2), (3))` MEANS
    `days after` `the days to notify and repay (s 20(2))` (`the earlier of` `the end of the period allowed for compliance` `and` `the date it first becomes apparent the requirement will not be complied with`)

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Grant party` `Grant act`
`s 20(2) -- notify the Commissioner and repay the grant within 14 days` MEANS
        (PARTY `the applicant`
         MUST  `give the Commissioner written notice that the residence requirement was not complied with`
         WITHIN `the days to notify and repay (s 20(2))`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "s 20(2)(a), (4): written notice to the Commissioner within 14 days after the relevant date; maximum penalty $5 000")
    RAND
        (PARTY `the applicant`
         MUST  `repay the amount of the grant`
         WITHIN `the days to notify and repay (s 20(2))`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "s 20(2)(b), (4): repay the grant within 14 days after the relevant date; maximum penalty $5 000, and a penalty up to the amount under s 39(3)")

-- What failing the requirement brings. If the grant was paid in anticipation, s 20(2); if not, the grant is simply
-- not payable (criterion 5, s 7(1)(a)), which the rule records as the requirement not met.
GIVEN `who must comply` IS A `Grant party`
      `the grant was paid in anticipation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Grant party` `Grant act`
`the consequence of failing the residence requirement (ss 7, 12, 20)` MEANS
    IF `the grant was paid in anticipation`
    THEN `s 20(2) -- notify the Commissioner and repay the grant within 14 days`
    ELSE BREACH BY `who must comply` BECAUSE "s 7(1)(a), s 12: the residence requirement is criterion 5; not met, no first home owner grant is payable"

-- The rule. Clock: days from the completion of the eligible transaction. `who must comply` is `the applicant` (each
-- applicant), or `a complying applicant, the others exempted by the Commissioner` where s 12(2) applies.
-- `the days in the completion period` and `the days in the residence period` come from the dates above.
GIVEN `who must comply` IS A `Grant party`
      `the days in the completion period` IS A NUMBER
      `the days in the residence period` IS A NUMBER
      `the grant was paid in anticipation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Grant party` `Grant act`
DECIDE `s 12 -- live in the home for 6 months, starting within 12 months after completion` IS
    PARTY  `who must comply`
    MUST   `begin to live in the home as the applicant's principal place of residence`
    WITHIN `the days in the completion period`
    HENCE
        PARTY  `who must comply`
        SHANT  `stop living in the home as the applicant's principal place of residence`
        WITHIN `the days in the residence period`
        HENCE  FULFILLED
        LEST   `the consequence of failing the residence requirement (ss 7, 12, 20)` `who must comply` `the grant was paid in anticipation`
    LEST   `the consequence of failing the residence requirement (ss 7, 12, 20)` `who must comply` `the grant was paid in anticipation`

§§ `ss 17, 24 -- the application and the decision (regulative)`

-- s 17(1): "If the Commissioner is satisfied that a grant authorised under this Act is payable on an application, the
-- Commissioner must authorise the payment of the grant." s 24(1): "When the Commissioner decides an application ... the
-- Commissioner must give the applicant notice of the decision." Applying is the applicant's choice, so not applying is
-- no breach (DO ... LEST FULFILLED); an application outside the s 14(5) period, unless the Commissioner allows it (s 14(6)),
-- obliges the Commissioner to nothing. Clock: days from the commencement date. No period is stated for the decision.
GIVEN `the days from the commencement date to the end of the application period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Grant party` `Grant act`
DECIDE `s 14(5) -- apply between the commencement date and 12 months after completion` IS
    PARTY  `the applicant`
    DO     `apply to the Commissioner for the grant`
    WITHIN `the days from the commencement date to the end of the application period`
    HENCE  (PARTY `the Commissioner of State Taxation`
            MUST  `give the applicant notice of the decision on the application`)
    LEST   FULFILLED

§§ `s 25, s 27, s 28 -- objection and review (regulative)`

-- s 25(1): an applicant "dissatisfied with the Commissioner's decision on the application", or with a decision "to
-- impose a penalty under section 39(2) or (3), may lodge a written notice of objection with the Treasurer". (2): grounds
-- "stated fully and in detail". (3): "lodged within 60 days after the date of the notice of the decision or, if the
-- decision was made in anticipation of a provision that operates retrospectively, within 60 days after the date of the
-- notice of the decision or the date of the enactment or making of the provision (whichever is the later)." (4): the
-- Treasurer may extend the time for a reasonable excuse. s 27(2): "The Treasurer must give the objector written notice of
-- the decision on the objection setting out the reasons". s 28(2): a review by SACAT "must be commenced within 60 days
-- after the notice of the decision on the objection is given (or such longer period as" SACAT allows).
`the days to object to a grant decision (s 25(3))` MEANS 60
`the days to seek a review by SACAT (s 28(2))` MEANS 60

GIVEN `the date of the notice of the decision` IS A DATE
      `the date the retrospective provision was enacted or made, if later` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to object to a grant decision (s 25(3))` MEANS
    `days after` `the days to object to a grant decision (s 25(3))` (`the later day`)
    WHERE
        `the later day` MEANS
            IF `the date the retrospective provision was enacted or made, if later` `is on or after` `the date of the notice of the decision`
            THEN `the date the retrospective provision was enacted or made, if later`
            ELSE `the date of the notice of the decision`

GIVEN `the days allowed to object` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Grant party` `Grant act`
DECIDE `s 25 -- object to the Treasurer within 60 days, then seek review within 60 days` IS
    PARTY  `the applicant`
    DO     `lodge a written notice of objection with the Treasurer`
    WITHIN `the days allowed to object`
    HENCE  (PARTY `the Treasurer`
            MUST  `give the objector written notice of the decision on the objection`
            HENCE (PARTY  `the applicant`
                   DO     `seek a review by the South Australian Civil and Administrative Tribunal`
                   WITHIN `the days to seek a review by SACAT (s 28(2))`
                   LEST   FULFILLED))
    LEST   FULFILLED

§§ `s 39 and s 40 -- repayment, penalty and recovery`

-- s 39(1): "The Commissioner may, by written notice, require an applicant (or former applicant) ... to repay an amount
-- paid on the application if -- (a) the amount was paid in error; or (b) the Commissioner reverses the decision under
-- which the amount was paid for any other reason." (2): if the amount was paid "as a result of the making of a false or
-- misleading statement by an applicant", the Commissioner may "impose a penalty not exceeding the amount the applicant is
-- required to repay". (3): if the applicant "fails to make a repayment required under this section or the conditions of
-- the grant, the Commissioner may, by written notice, impose a penalty not exceeding the amount the applicant is required
-- to repay."
GIVEN `the amount was paid in error` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner reverses the decision under which it was paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `repayment of the grant can be required (s 39(1))` IF
        `the amount was paid in error`
    OR  `the Commissioner reverses the decision under which it was paid`

-- READING (NOTES.md, finding 15): (2) and (3) are separate powers, each capped at the amount to be repaid; where both
-- grounds arise, the most is the two together.
GIVEN `the amount required to be repaid` IS A NUMBER
      `it was paid because of a false or misleading statement by an applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant failed to make the repayment required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most penalty under s 39(2) and (3)` MEANS
        (IF `it was paid because of a false or misleading statement by an applicant` THEN `the amount required to be repaid` ELSE 0)
    PLUS (IF `the applicant failed to make the repayment required` THEN `the amount required to be repaid` ELSE 0)

-- The repayment as a rule. s 39 states no period: the notice states it (s 21(2)(b) likewise for conditions). Clock: days
-- from the notice. Failing it, the Commissioner may impose the s 39(3) penalty (a discretion, so the most is stated).
GIVEN `the days the notice allows` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Grant party` `Grant act`
DECIDE `s 39 -- repay the amount the Commissioner's notice requires` IS
    PARTY  `the applicant`
    MUST   `repay the amount required by the notice`
    WITHIN `the days the notice allows`
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "s 39(3): the repayment required was not made; the Commissioner may by written notice impose a penalty not exceeding the amount, recoverable as a debt due to the Crown and a first charge on the applicant's interest in the land (s 40(3), (4))"

-- s 40(2): "The liability arising from a requirement to pay (or repay) an amount to which this section applies is, if
-- the requirement attaches to 2 or more persons, joint and several." (3): if the applicant has "an interest in the land
-- on which the home was built or was to be built, the liability is a first charge on the applicant's interest in that
-- land." (4): recoverable "as a debt due to the Crown". (5): the Commissioner may arrange payment "by instalments", with
-- interest. Regulations 2015, reg 6(2): "the sum of -- (a) the market rate; and (b) 8% per annum"; the market rate (reg
-- 6(3)) is the May average of the 90-day Bank Accepted Bill Rate or a gazetted rate -- an INPUT.
DECLARE `How a repayment is owed` IS ONE OF
    `by the one applicant, as a debt due to the Crown`
    `jointly and severally by the applicants, as a debt due to the Crown`

GIVEN `the number of applicants required to repay` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `How a repayment is owed`
`how the repayment is owed (s 40(2), (4))` MEANS
    IF `the number of applicants required to repay` GREATER THAN 1
    THEN `jointly and severally by the applicants, as a debt due to the Crown`
    ELSE `by the one applicant, as a debt due to the Crown`

GIVEN `the applicant has an interest in the land on which the home was or was to be built` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the repayment is a first charge on the applicant's interest in the land (s 40(3))` IF
    `the applicant has an interest in the land on which the home was or was to be built`

`the premium on instalment interest, per cent a year (reg 6(2)(b))` MEANS 8

GIVEN `the market rate, per cent a year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the interest rate on repayment by instalments, per cent a year (reg 6)` MEANS
    `the market rate, per cent a year` PLUS `the premium on instalment interest, per cent a year (reg 6(2)(b))`
